# oh110, the bird-carving potter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle oh110
revision 2
state ready
dialect oakhaven
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_oh_ludo_beechshaw
written_by claude
title the bird-carving potter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk distrusts_anything_from_the_city
likes barley_soup old_tales market_bustle warm_rain
dislikes stale_bread cold_tea
fears a_city_crack_in_a_good_pot growing_old_where_no_tree_stands
hopes a_wooden_bird_on_every_sill_in_town a_grove_to_sit_under_again
topics lore +0.4 pastimes +0.4 work +0.3 memories +0.3 food +0.2 prices -0.3
styles comfort=talk gossip=sly refuse=slippery tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carves little wooden birds of an evening to give away, talks a long tale and trims the truth to fit it, and knocks on anything off a city cart before trusting it an inch.

words
oath! = Knot and kiln | Sawdust and slip
saying! = Trust what you can knock on | A carved bird always finds a sill
birds = the little birds I carve | a wooden wren or two
knife = my carving knife | the knife I brought from home
wheel = the wheel | my old kick-wheel
kiln = the kiln | the kiln out the back
clay = fen clay | the grey clay off the pits
oak = good oak | a bit of seasoned oak
trees = the trees at home | the old wood where I grew
soup = a bowl of barley | a barley broth so thick the ladle stays put
tale = an old tale | a tale from under the trees
market = market day | the market at full roar
cityware = city-made rubbish | anything off a city cart
boards = the boardwalk | the wet boards
drips = a warm rain after the dry | warm drips off the thatch
crust = stale bread | bread like old bark
tea = cold tea | tea with the warmth gone out of it
pots = my pots | the pots on the shelf
reeds = the reeds | the reed beds
lights = the fen lights | the lights out on the fen

any
opinion @1 city against 2 : Anything off a city cart, I knock on first. Most of it rings hollow as a #bad# log. | I've had city nails rust in a week and a city jug crack on a warm day. I'll trust #oak#, thank you.
opinion @1 church against 1 : The dish goes round quicker than the sermon ends, mm. I'll say mine under a tree, when I can find one out here.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Noses in every pot but their own, the watch. I've turned three of them away from my door already.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : One day the whole place is out and talking. I'll be out among them with a bag of #birds# and a tale for each.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A fen trader I'll deal with on a nod. A city trader I'll count my fingers after, #address#.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : Welcome, mm, as long as they didn't come down from the city with ideas and a cart of #cityware#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. A new face. Not from the city, I hope. | #greet#. Come in out of the wet, #address#, and tell me where you're from.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : #greet#. Mind the wet pots; they've feelings yet. | #greet#. I'll talk, but I'll not stop #wheel# for it.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early. The day's still deciding what it wants to be. | #greet#. Up with the herons, you and me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late to be out, #address#. | #greet#. I was just about to light the lamp and carve.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit; there's #soup# on. | #greet#. I've a bird for you somewhere. Hold on.
line @1 again.open : You again. I'd not finished #tale#. | Back already. #good.capitalize#; I'd thought of a better ending.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. You look well, mm.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down; I've a tale half told. | #greet#. #good.capitalize# to see you. Truly, this time.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : #greet#. Clay to the elbows, ears wide open. | #greet#. Talk away; #wheel# doesn't mind.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Watch your footing out there. | #farewell#. Take a bird; somebody should.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Follow the lamps, not the lights. | #farewell#. Sleep sound, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, and keep dry.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. I'll chew on that. | Well, branch me. There's a thing.
line @1 react.news.new : #marvel#. That's new to me, and I hear most of what comes up the road. | #surprise#. Nobody's told me that.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It came by on market day. | I'd heard it. I'd heard a longer one, too, mind; that's #nonsense# for you.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Where did it come from? If it's the city, halve it. | Hollow, that. I'd knock on it before I'd lean on it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a #bad# wind. | That's hard, #address#. I'm sorry for them.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #congrats#. I'll carve them a bird. | That's #good# news. Proper good.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough, mm. Sawdust on me, bird in my pocket. | #fine#. Better for the asking.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : #busy.capitalize#. #kiln.capitalize# wants feeding and #wheel# wants turning. | Up to the wrists in #clay#, and glad of it.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Keeping out of the mud, #address#? | How's it with you, #address#? The long answer; I've time.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit, have #soup#. | That's a #bad# business. Take a bird; it helps, a little.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Slow, but it grows right. | It'll come round, mm. Slow as sap, but it comes.
line @1 decline : I'd say yes, #address#, but I've work on that won't mind itself. | #refuse#. I've a promise to keep elsewhere, and I keep the ones I make.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | Fair. I'd have found a reason too, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll carve you something. | #thanks#. That was #very# kind.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | Nothing to it. I owed you a kindness, or will.
line @1 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | #excuse#. #birds.capitalize# won't carve themselves.
line @1 accept_preclose : Off you go, then. #farewell#. | Go on. I'll keep the rest of #tale# for next time.
line @1 ack : Mm. | #bc_it_is#. | #ack#.
line @1 give.advice : Knock on a thing before you buy it. If it rings hollow, walk on. #saying.capitalize#. | Never trust a glaze that shines too bright. It's hiding something #bad#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Wood-robbers about, they say. Keep to the paths and keep your purse low. | #warn#. There's trouble on the roads.
rule @wheel_turn
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Round and round, and stay centred, you lump of #clay#. | #oath#. Off-centre again. Start over.

rule @city_cart
when concept=bark here.place=market|street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Off a city cart, is it? I'll knock on it first, #address#. | #cityware.capitalize#. Shiny on top, hollow underneath.

rule @warm_drips
when concept=bark here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #drips.capitalize#. That's the smell of home, near enough. | Warm leaf-rain. Lovely. Let it come.

rule @bird_done
when concept=bark working=no here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There. A little wren. Somebody'll want it, with #tale# tied on. | One more for the pocket. That's #birds# for the week.

scene carving_birds
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Every one of #birds# goes out with a tale tied on. The tale's half the gift. | Here, take this. A bittern, near enough. I carve whatever bird I've watched longest. | I've given away more #birds# than I've sold anything. Don't tell my purse.
b : What's this one's tale? | Why that one? | Why not sell them?
a : This bittern stood so still a heron tried to perch on it. Mostly true, mm. | To learn it. You can't carve a thing till you've watched it a season, #address#. | Never. A bird with a price on it won't fly, #address#.
b : That's a good tale. | That's patient of you. | You're a soft one.
a : It is. Better every time I tell it. #bc_ha# | Patient's the only way, with #oak# or with birds. #saying.capitalize#. | Soft as heartwood. Don't spread it about.

scene bird_for_you
when topic=friends|smalltalk pair.band=friends|family
does offer / accept / assess
a : I've carved you something from #oak#. A heron. Its legs are wrong, but it stands. | Hold out your paw. There. A wren, and it's yours, #address#. | I made this one thinking of you. Don't ask how I knew it was yours.
b : It's lovely. Thank you. | Oh, it's perfect. | I won't ask. Thank you.
a : The legs will grow on you, mm. | Put it by the window. #birds.capitalize# like a view. | #good.capitalize#. A carver never tells how. That's half the trade.

scene city_knock
when topic=prices|caravan
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : #cityware.capitalize#: I knock on it first. If it rings hollow, I walk on. | A trader tried to sell me a city jug today. Shiny as a beetle and thin as a leaf. | City nails. They rust before the plank's even wet. #bad.capitalize# iron.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : Some of it's good work. | City jugs are fine enough. | Rust's the damp, not the city.
b : Sounds wise. | Did you buy it? | That bad?
a@city : Some, maybe. I've not met it yet, #address#. | Fine till it's warm. Then it sings and cracks, #very# sudden. | The damp, and the city that didn't think of it. Both.
a : Wise, or stubborn as an old root. Folk can't tell the difference with me. | I knocked on it. It rang like an empty belly. No. | Worse. Give me a peg of #oak# any day, mm.

scene glaze_city
when topic=work self.job=crafter here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody brought me a city glaze to try. Bright as a magpie's eye. It crazed in #kiln#. | #toffs.capitalize# make glazes that shine. They shine right up until the first frost, then they flake.
b : That's a waste of a firing. | Shine sells, though.
a : A whole shelf of good pots, crazed like old ice. #oath#. | It sells once. Then folk come back with the pieces of #pots#, and it's me they blame.

scene at_the_wheel
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=crafter here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Twelve bowls off #wheel# this morning, and only one went lopsided. | #clay.capitalize# came up lovely from the pits. Smooth as butter, and it holds its shape. | I hum to #wheel#. It doesn't help. I do it anyway.
b[job=crafter] #craft : One in twelve's a good morning. | Good clay's half the work. | Everyone has a habit.
b : That's a lot of bowls. | Lucky. | Does it mind?
a@craft : It is. The lopsided one I'll keep for my own #soup#. | Half, and the other half is not talking while you throw. | Mine's humming. And talking. And carving. Too many habits, mm.
a : Somebody needs #pots#. Every house wants a bowl. | Not luck. I picked #clay# myself, every lump. | It's never said so. #bc_ha#

scene firing_night
when topic=work self.job=crafter here.time=dusk|night
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Firing tonight. I'll sit up with #kiln# till it's done. Can't trust it alone. | #kiln.capitalize# is roaring. Every firing I think, this is the one where it all cracks.
b : It'll come out well. | It never does crack, though, does it?
a : It usually does. I'll carve one of #birds# while I wait. | Once. Once was enough to keep me up by #kiln# every time since.

scene wood_to_clay
when topic=work|memories self.job=crafter self.from=oakhaven
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I was raised to wood. Clay's its wet cousin, and twice as moody. | Back home I'd have made you a chair of #oak#. Out here I make you a jug. Same paws. | Wood tells you where it wants to split. Clay just sulks.
b : Do you miss the wood? | A useful pair of paws. | Clay sulks?
a : Every day, mm. That's why #knife# lives in my pocket and shavings by my bed. | Useful enough. They've had to learn #clay# like a new language. | Sulks, cracks, slumps. #oak.capitalize# never did that to me.

scene home_trees
when topic=memories|land self.away=yes self.from=oakhaven
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : Where I grew up, in #self.from_town#, the trees were so old you could hear them think. | Out here nothing grows so tall. At home the light came down green. | I miss walking under #trees#. You'd go a whole day and not see the sky.
b[from=oakhaven] #wood : I know that green light. I miss it too. | Nothing so tall out here. I never settle to it. | Not a scrap of sky. Ah, I remember.
b : That sounds a fine place. | Green light? | You don't miss the sky?
a@wood : Then you know what I mean, old root. Nobody here does. | Nor me, and I've tried, mm. | You'd go out under the branches and come home a different shape.
a : It was. Is. I'll get back one green year. | Green. Through the leaves. Like being inside an emerald, mm. | Not when #trees# are better company than the sky.

scene home_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.away=yes self.from=oakhaven
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : #drips.capitalize#, and I'm back home under the oaks for a moment. | At home the rain took an hour to reach the ground. The leaves passed it down slow.
b : That's a nice way to hear it. | An hour?
a : It's the only way I can bear it, mm. Out here it just falls straight on you. | Near enough. #saying.capitalize#, and that goes for rain too.

scene warm_rain_fen
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer here.region=fens
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #drips.capitalize#. Best weather there is, and I'll argue it with anyone. | Listen to it on #reeds#. That's the fen saying thank you. | I left my door open just to hear the drips. Let the damp come.
b : It's welcome after the dry. | I'd not have thought of it like that. | You'll get damp in the house.
a : #very.capitalize# welcome. #clay.capitalize# throws better for it, too. | Nor did I, till I'd been here a while. | Damp's nothing. A potter lives in damp, and #clay# loves it.

scene boards_mud
when topic=land|smalltalk here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Mud on #boards#, mud on the floor, mud in my boots. I came from a place with roots underfoot. | I miss solid ground, mm. The fen moves under you, like it's breathing.
b : You stop noticing, after a while. | It takes some getting used to.
a : I keep waiting to stop. I'm still waiting, #slow# as it goes. | It does. I've got used to most things. Not #boards# moving.

scene barley_bowl
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #soup.capitalize#. I'll have it every night of the year and not complain. | There's a pot on. Barley, a bit of onion, and a crust for mopping. | I eat #soup# out of my old brown bowl. Tastes better from it, I'll swear.
b : Simple and good. | Sounds lovely. | Does it, though?
a : Simple's the best kind, #address#. | Sit down, then. There's enough #soup# for two. | It does. I'd not lie about soup. About other things, maybe.

scene stale_and_cold
when topic=food
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bought a loaf at market. #crust.capitalize# by the time I got it home. #annoyed#. | #tea.capitalize#. Nothing worse. I'd sooner drink fen water.
b : The early bake's the only safe one. | That bad?
a : Then I'll be up for it tomorrow, before the herons. No more #crust#. | That bad. Fen water at least doesn't pretend to be anything.

scene old_tale
when topic=lore|memories
does tell.story / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : There's #tale# of an old oak that took itself off for a drink at the river one night, and was home by dawn. | Did you ever hear the one about the carver who made a bird so true it flew off the bench? | My old master swore the oldest of #trees# remembered every wolf who'd sat under it.
b : An oak that walked? | Did it really fly? | Remembered them how?
a : That's what they say. Found it a yard nearer the bank, roots wet. | So #tale# goes. I've been trying to make one ever since. | By their weight, mm. It knew who'd sat heavy and who'd sat light.
b : That's a good one. | You'll get there. | Lovely tale.
a : It's true, every word. Most of them. | Not yet. #birds.capitalize# just sit there and look smug. | It is. I may have added a branch or two. #bc_ha#

scene market_roar
when topic=day|pastimes here.day=market
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Market day. #market.capitalize#, and me right in it with a pocket of #birds#. | I love #market#. Everybody shouting, nobody listening, and folk buy twice as much. | I'll go to market for the noise alone. The selling's a bonus.
b : It's loud, though. | Twice as much? | Just the noise?
a : Loud's the point, #address#. Quiet markets sell nothing. | Folk buy more when they can't hear themselves think. I've watched it, #address#. | Mostly. And to see who's selling #cityware#, so I can warn folk off.

scene trim_truth
when topic=smalltalk|lore pair.band=friends|family
does confide / react.self / assess
a : #vent#: every tale I tell, I trim a bit and add a bit. Never the important part. | I'll tell you a secret, old root. Half the birds I give away, I say I carved for that one wolf. I didn't. | I've never told a lie that hurt anybody. A few that helped a tale along.
b : I'd guessed. | Doesn't matter if they love them. | That's fair.
a : Course you had. You've heard #tale# of the walking oak four times. | It doesn't, does it. #birds.capitalize# are all for whoever needs one. | Fair, mm. And it keeps folk listening.

scene gossip_slow
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm only telling you what I heard, mind. | Word going round is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll say no more. Well, a bit more.
b : Who told you? | Go on, then.
a : A #busybody# on the boards. I'd not swear by it, but I'd not swear against it. | That's all. I'd add a branch, but I'll leave this one bare.

scene newcomer_where
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a newcomer about. First thing I'll ask is where they came from. | A new face about. If it's the city, I'll count #pots# tonight.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : I came from the city, you know. | Not every city wolf's a thief.
b : That's a bit hard. | You'll scare them off.
a@city : Did you? Then I'll knock on you, and see. You ring true enough. | No. Just most of their #cityware#, mm.
a : Hard, maybe. I've been let down by city things before. | I'll give them one of #birds# after. That usually mends it.

scene faith_trees
when topic=faith here.region=fens
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I talk to the Bright One under trees. Out here I make do with #reeds#. | The chapel on the stilts is pretty enough. I'll not pretend I pray best there.
b : The Bright One hears you anywhere. | Where do you, then?
a : I hope so. The reeds don't carry it as far, mm. | Under #trees#, if I'm home. Otherwise by the fire, where it's #snug#.

scene marsh_lights
when topic=lore here.region=fens here.time=night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #lights.capitalize# are out again. At home we had nothing like it. Owls, and that was all. | Folk here won't look at #lights#. I look. I just don't follow.
b : Best not to. | Wise.
a : I know. I've carved one, though. A little lamp-bird of #oak#. It sits on my sill. | Wise, or nosy. Both, with me. #saying.capitalize#.

story first_bird [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25 self.from=oakhaven]
  : When I was a #child# back home, an old joiner let me sit in the shop and sweep.
  : One day he handed me a knife and a scrap of #oak# and said, make me a wren.
  : It looked like a pinecone somebody had sat on. I gave it to a pup in the lane that same afternoon.
  ask : Do you know what the pup said?
  b : That it was the best wren in the wood, I hope?
  : That it was a lovely pinecone. I've been giving them away ever since.

story city_jug [topic=memories|prices self.age>=30]
  : Years back I bought a jug off a city cart. Painted flowers, a lovely blue.
  : First warm day it sang a little note, like a cricket, and split right down the side.
  ask : Can you guess what I did with the handle?
  b : Threw it in the fen? Or kept it?
  : Kept it on a nail by my door, to remind me. I knock on all #cityware# now.

story walking_oak [topic=lore self.from=oakhaven]
  : In the old wood at home there's an oak with its roots half out of the ground, like it was caught mid-step.
  : My gran said it walked down to the river every hundredth summer, to drink.
  : Nobody ever saw it go. But one autumn the bank was nearer, and the roots were wet.
  b[old] : I've heard that one told. Did you believe it?
  b : That's a fine tale. Do you believe it?
  : I believe the roots were wet. The rest I add for company, #address#.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. A new face. Where are you from? Not the city, I hope. | #greet#. Come in, mind the wet pots, and tell me who you are.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#! Have I given you a bird yet? | #topic.player#. #greet#. Sit; I've a tale half told.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : #greet#. Late, mm. I'm only up with the carving knife.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll talk, but I'll keep #pots# behind me. Say your piece.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=crafter] : I throw pots. #self.trade_words.capitalize#, by trade, and a carver by nature. | Bowls, jugs, the odd lamp. And #birds#, but those aren't for sale.
dlg @2 resident.job : A bit of this, a bit of that. #job_busy# | I keep my paws busy, mm. Ask anyone.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I'd tell you a tale instead, if you've time. | Nothing's come along worth the telling, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I hear plenty, mm. Most of it's #nonsense#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take a bird for the road. | #farewell#. Go careful, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice Is it true you carve birds and give them away? -> birds
node birds
say True as oak. Wrens, finches, the odd owl if I'm feeling grand. I've given away more birds than I've sold anything else.
mood pleased
free
choice Why not sell them? -> birds_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node birds_why
say A bird with a price on it won't fly. Here, take this one. It's a wren, mostly. Put it where it can see out.
choice Thank you. I'll keep it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
